      "id": 30, "type": "Note", "pos": [0, 620], "size": [700, 300], "flags": {}, "order": 29, "mode": 0,
      "inputs": [], "outputs": [], "properties": {},
      "widgets_values": [
        "LORA PIXEL SPRITE - FIXED 128x128 OUTPUT\n\nThis is real SDXL img2img, not a nearest-neighbor filter.\n\nInstalled stack: SDXL Base + pixel-art-xl LoRA + SDXL Tile ControlNet + downloaded pixel 1 palette.\nThe LoRA trigger pixelbuildings128 must remain in the positive prompt.\n\nPreserve defaults: LoRA 0.80, ControlNet 0.65, denoise 0.38, fixed seed 42.\nLower denoise toward 0.28 for a more literal source copy; raise it only if more redesign is acceptable. The final alpha always follows the original silhouette.\n\nThe source white background creates alpha after generation, so pale colors from the palette remain visible. Output is one 128x128 RGBA PNG on a logical 64x64 pixel grid."
      ],
      "color": "#243", "bgcolor": "#465"
    }
